From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: nmcli Wi-Fi driver: no shell for SSIDs

Backport of upstream RetroArch 8e0f4ae0acf4 "nmcli: avoid shell execution
from nearby SSIDs (#19646)", 2026-10-01, which v1.22.2 does not have.

While listing Wi-Fi networks, the nmcli driver put every SSID it found
into a system() command in single quotes. An access point in range named
with a quote could run commands as the RetroArch user (ark, with sudo) as
soon as the list was opened, without connecting. Connecting and
disconnecting did the same with the SSID and the passphrase. nmcli is now
started with posix_spawnp and its arguments as they are.

